README.md-1-# .dotfiles
README.md-2-
README.md-3-A single minimal `seed.wsl` is published from every push to `master`. Importing it
README.md-4-gives you a tiny NixOS-WSL bootstrap that, on first interactive login, asks
README.md:5:which identity to take and `nixos-rebuild boot`s into it.
README.md-6-
README.md-7-## Install (NixOS-WSL)
README.md-8-
README.md-9-From Windows PowerShell:
README.md-10-```powershell
README.md-11-$tarball = "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\seed.wsl"
README.md-12-Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/releases/latest/download/seed.wsl" -OutFile $tarball
README.md-13-wsl --import thixos "$env:USERPROFILE\WSL\thixos" $tarball
README.md-14-wsl -d thixos
README.md-15-# → at the prompt, type `t` for thixos or `y` for yoloixos (YOLO to confirm)
README.md-16-# → seed stages the chosen config and terminates the distro
README.md-17-wsl -d thixos
README.md-18-# → boots into the chosen identity; init-gh / init-yolo completes setup
README.md-19-```
README.md-20-
README.md-21-## Architecture
README.md-22-
README.md-23-- `seed` — minimal bootstrap; bash login, NOPASSWD wheel sudo, `inputs.self`
README.md:24:  baked at `/etc/seed-source`. Prompts t/y, runs `nixos-rebuild switch --flake
README.md-25-  /etc/seed-source#<choice>` (switch, not boot — activation must rewrite
README.md-26-  `/etc/wsl.conf` *now* so the next launch finds the new default user), marks
README.md-27-  `/var/lib/seed-bootstrap.done`, then `wsl.exe --terminate $WSL_DISTRO_NAME`.
README.md-28-- `thixos` — interactive dev. User `thom` (wheel), Tailscale, full toolchain.
README.md-29-- `yoloixos` — agent sandbox. User `agent` (no wheel), no interop, no
README.md-30-  automount, outbound firewall, 4GB / 200% CPU slice. **One-way: `agent` has
README.md-31-  no sudo, so the image can never be rebuilt.**
README.md-32-
README.md-33-## Update
README.md-34-
README.md-35-Inside thixos:
README.md-36-```shell
README.md:37:sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles#thixos
README.md-38-```
README.md-39-(Inside yoloixos this is intentionally impossible.)
README.md-40-
README.md-41-## WSL networking and authentication
README.md-42-
README.md-43-`config/wslconfig` selects Consomme. Mirrored mode previously dropped the guest's
README.md-44-default route on Wi-Fi NIC events, so switching back can reintroduce that problem.
README.md-45-
README.md-46-Firebase's browser login normally opens a dual-stack `[::]` callback listener.
README.md-47-Consomme currently refuses IPv4 connections to that listener and hangs forwarding
README.md-48-IPv6 from Windows ([WSL#41860](https://github.com/microsoft/WSL/issues/41860)).
README.md-49-`home/home.nix` patches Firebase to listen on `127.0.0.1` instead; both
README.md-50-`firebase login --reauth` and `gcloud-reauth` use that package. Firebase also
README.md-51-picks its port by binding and instantly closing it on every local address.
README.md-52-Consomme keeps a phantom listener for each probe for about a minute, and a real
README.md-53-bind that follows on the same port is silently moved to a random port when one
README.md-54-side is a wildcard and the other a specific address of the same family (0.0.0.0
README.md-55-against 127.0.0.1, `::` against `::1`). The login redirect to `localhost:9005`
README.md-56-then finds nothing and the CLI waits forever, so the patch probes only
README.md-57-`127.0.0.1`. The substitutions fail the build if upstream changes either spot,
README.md-58-so the workaround gets reviewed on upgrades. Before rebuilding,
README.md-59-`firebase login --reauth --no-localhost` bypasses the callback entirely using
README.md-60-Firebase's supported code-paste flow. Agent shells get that flow regardless:
README.md-61-Firebase treats `CLAUDECODE` and similar variables as non-interactive. Run the
README.md-62-login from a normal pane, or add `--interactive`.
README.md-63-
README.md-64-Node dev servers hit the same wall. `listen(port)` with no host binds `[::]`, so
README.md-65-Windows Chrome gets `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` from, for example,
README.md-66-`https://app-local.dev.bookcreator.com:3000`. `config/node/ipv4-listen.js` is
README.md-67-preloaded into every Node process started from zsh (`NODE_OPTIONS`, set in
README.md-68-`home/shell.nix`) and makes a host-less `listen` bind `0.0.0.0` instead. Servers
README.md-69-that pass a host are untouched and `NODE_LISTEN_DUALSTACK=1` switches the shim
README.md-70-off. It does not cover servers that are not Node, or Node started outside zsh or
README.md-71-with its own `NODE_OPTIONS`. The `*-local.dev.bookcreator.com` names point at
README.md-72-localhost through `networking.hosts` on thixos and, for Windows, through the
--
README.md-123-
README.md-124-On Windows (admin PowerShell) — install the USB/IP daemon and share the probe:
README.md-125-```powershell
README.md-126-winget install usbipd
README.md-127-usbipd list                  # note the BUSID of your probe, e.g. 3-1
README.md-128-usbipd bind --busid <BUSID>  # plain bind — NOT --force (see Troubleshooting)
README.md-129-```
README.md-130-Set `autoAttach = [ "<BUSID>" ];` in `nixos/embedded.nix`, rebuild, then restart
README.md-131-WSL once (the restart loads `vhci_hcd` and applies the `plugdev` group):
README.md-132-```shell
README.md:133:sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles#thixos
README.md-134-```
README.md-135-```powershell
README.md-136-wsl --shutdown               # from Windows; reopen thixos afterwards
README.md-137-```
README.md-138-
README.md-139-### Day-to-day (hands-off)
README.md-140-
README.md-141-Nothing — a systemd service (`usbip-auto-attach@<BUSID>`) polls every second and
README.md-142-(re)attaches the probe across boots, replugs and resets. Confirm with `lsusb`
README.md-143-(probe shows up, e.g. `2e8a:000c`). Manual override: `usbip-attach [VID:PID]`.
README.md-144-
README.md-145-### The toolchain (in your project, not the dotfiles)
README.md-146-
README.md-147-probe-rs is intentionally not system-installed — add it to the project devshell:
README.md-148-```nix
README.md-149-devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
README.md-150-  packages = [ pkgs.probe-rs-tools /* + rust toolchain, flip-link, … */ ];
README.md-151-};
README.md-152-```
README.md-153-Then `probe-rs list` sees the probe (via the system udev rule) and you flash with
README.md-154-`probe-rs run --chip RP235x <elf>` (`probe-rs chip list | grep -i rp235` for the
README.md-155-exact chip name).
README.md-156-
README.md-157-### Troubleshooting (lessons learned)
README.md-158-
README.md-159-- **Never `usbipd bind --force`.** It permanently swaps the device onto usbipd's
README.md-160-  VBoxUSB stub driver; it then flip-flops ("Shared (forced)" toggling) and the WSL
README.md-161-  attach alternates *"Device in error state"/"not found"*. Use plain `bind`. To
README.md-162-  recover a stuck device: Device Manager → Uninstall device → unplug/replug, then
README.md-163-  plain `bind`. If plain `bind` won't hold, a USB filter driver (real VirtualBox, or
README.md-164-  RDP/AV USB redirection) is claiming it — remove that.
README.md-165-- **Not in `lsusb`, `usbip port` says "is vhci_hcd loaded?"** → the module didn't
README.md-166-  load. It's `boot.kernelModules = [ "vhci_hcd" ]`; needs a `wsl --shutdown` (or
README.md-167-  `sudo modprobe vhci_hcd` to load immediately).
README.md-168-- **Can't reach the server** (`usbip list -r 127.0.0.1` fails) → Windows Firewall
--
README.md-192-## Spawn a new WSL distro from inside thixos
README.md-193-
README.md-194-Open the session-picker and press **Ctrl+Y** ("Create from seed"). It prompts
README.md-195-for a name, downloads the latest `seed.wsl` from GitHub Releases, runs
README.md-196-`wsl.exe --import`, and launches it — landing you back at the t/y prompt
README.md-197-inside the new distro. Locally-installed distros also show up in the
README.md-198-session-picker (`wsl/<name>`) for quick attach.
README.md-199-
README.md-200-## Install (Ubuntu / Non-NixOS Standalone)
README.md-201-
README.md:202:Just the home-manager profile, no system-level isolation:
README.md-203-```shell
README.md-204-sh <(curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install) --daemon
README.md-205-echo "trusted-users = root $USER" | sudo tee -a /etc/nix/nix.conf
README.md-206-sudo systemctl restart nix-daemon
README.md-207-mkdir -p ~/.config/nix && echo "experimental-features = nix-command flakes" >> ~/.config/nix/nix.conf
README.md-208-mkdir -p ~/src/github.com/tteggel
README.md-209-git clone https://github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles.git ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles
README.md:210:MINIMAL_ENV=1 nix run home-manager/master -- switch --impure -b backup \
README.md-211-  --flake ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles#thom@nix
README.md-212-# then, once the binary cache has primed, the full env:
README.md:213:home-manager switch --impure -b backup --flake ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles#thom@nix
README.md-214-```
README.md-215-Swap `thom@nix` for `agent@nix` to take the restricted agent profile (no
README.md-216-infrastructure tools; relies on shell-level discipline, not kernel
README.md-217-isolation).

